-- title:
--   Strict bundle-boundary counts equal source-full boundary mass
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ and $K$ be finite sets, let $k,r$ be natural numbers, let $P$ be an ordered coarse–fine complex on $G$, and let $A$ be a closed ordered atom configuration for its coarse complex. Let $B$ be a hypergraph bundle over the ordered-configuration base edges, with occurrence edges closed under inclusion. For every nonempty occurrence edge $g_0$ of $B$,
--   $$
--   \operatorname{count}_{\partial_{<g_0}B}(w_A)
--   =\mathbb E\bigl[W^{\mathrm{source}}_{P,A}(f_{g_0},\,\cdot\,)\bigr].
--   $$
--   The left side is the bundle count on the strict boundary using the pulled-back configuration base weight $w_A$. The right side is the normalized mean of the source-full mixed boundary weight on the associated ordered configuration face.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs/blob/8822f7ddef30fadbd92e1c6ab4ed897af356af5e/src/latest/Wikipedia/SzemeredisTheorem/Hypergraph/HypergraphBundleSourceGoodnessBridge.lean#L720-L821

